> Indonesia - E[ko Nug]roho and "Wayang Bocor"
Eko Nurgoho is one of Indonesia's[ most provocative young] artists[ whose] style is a unique mix of Indonesia's rich traditions and popular culture[ t]inged[ with] dark[ humor]. Using a distinctive blend of high and low art,[ Nug]roho' "Wayang Bocor" is a contemporary form of theater in which puppets and actors weave[ together] traditional elements of Indonesian 'way[ag]' (shadow puppets) with[ live] theater and scripts[ that] cast a[ satiric] view of[ contemporary subjects]. The show "God Bliss" tells[ the] story of how Islam[ came] to Java, and[ became] absorbed as part of Javanese culture[ that] includes elements of Hinduism, Buddhism, and animism. Sim[ultaneously playful] and[ penetrating].[][][][][][][][][][]

