> Why does your body grow healthy[ …] or unhealthy cells?
Home » Blog » Why does your body grow healthy[ …] or unhealthy cells?
Look outside and see how[ fast] your garden is turning green. Spring[ acceler]ates cellular growth. When cells multiply and divide, they duplicate their present condition. When mutated[ cells] divide, they recreate their chaos and[ continue] to do[ so].
How can you create[ healthy cells] in a habitat of[ pollution]? A body full of toxic wastes, heavy metals, and acidic chemicals is providing a perfect habitat for destructive[ microbes]. When they take over,[ microbes] create mutations inside your[ cells].[ Vir]uses,[ fungus], and[ bad microbes] love[ toxic] waste. They not only survive on it, but they also[ thrive] on it!
Harmony and[ wellness] need a pure, clean,[ healthy] environment. Excess[ acidic] wastes are the underlying cause of degener[ative diseases] such as[ diabetes],[ arthritis],[ fibromyalgia],[ r]he[umat]oid[ arthritis], neurological[ disorders], and cancer, in fact, all other[ diseases].
